The '''Imperial Security Bureau safe room''' was a room in the [[Imperial office complex]] located near the [[Palmo Plaza]] in [[Palmo]], the [[capital]] [[city]] of the [[planet]] [[Ghorman]]. The soundproof room provided a secure direct connection to [[Coruscant]]. In [[3 BBY]] [[Syril Karn]] used while working undercover as the [[Division Chief]] of the local [[Imperial Bureau of Standards]] [[Bureau of Standards Ghorman field office|field office]] to contact [[ISB Supervisor]] [[Dedra Meero]] to inform her that he made contact with the [[Ghorman Front]], a local rebel cell.<ref name="Ever Been to Ghorman" /> Dedra retreated to the room after the [[Ghorman Massacre]].<ref name="Who Are You?">{{Andor|Who Are You?}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The safe room appeared in the [[Andor Season 2|second season]] of the live-action series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'', first appearing in the series's fourth episode, "[[Ever Been to Ghorman?]]," which was released on [[Disney+]]<ref name="Ever Been to Ghorman" /> on [[April 29]], [[2025]].<ref name="Trailer News">{{SW|url=news/andor-season-2-teaser-trailer-key-art-reveal|text=First ''Andor A Star Wars Story'' Teaser Trailer and Poster Revealed}}</ref> A [[Databank (2014-)|Star Wars Databank]] entry for the safe room was added on the same day.<ref name="Safe room databank">{{Databank|imperial-security-bureau-safe-room|Imperial Security Bureau safe room}}</ref>

